5. MEMORY ≠ TRUTH

This is arguably the most powerful conceptual invention in the whole system.

A Smart Note isn't automatically truth.

A memory object needs:

source
timestamp
authority
evidence
freshness
applicability
supersession
relationships
semantic aliases

And different knowledge needs different decay behavior.

For example:

Architecture decision

→ may remain valid until explicitly superseded.

Deployment state

→ may become stale within hours.

Test result

→ may become invalid the moment the relevant artifact changes.

Preference

→ may remain useful for months but eventually deserve reconfirmation.

That distinction was one of the strongest recommendations in the independent review.

This is how we prevent:

"Naya remembers something"

from becoming:

"Naya believes something forever."

